# Provenance — charts/README.md § `SOURCE` is required, including when nothing was forked.
#
# ADR-010: "Their charts are a starting point, not a dependency. Where a chart is close, fork it into
# charts/ with the upstream commit recorded in a SOURCE file." Nothing was forked here — Kube-OVN is
# platform infrastructure installed once per cluster (ADR-019) and what this chart renders is a
# tenant's row in that installation — and `vendored: none` is an answer to "where did this come from"
# where a missing file is not.

vendored: none
upstream: https://github.com/kubeovn/kube-ovn

# The upstream API this chart's template targets. ⚠ An API group/version, not a commit: nothing is
# vendored, so there is no upstream tree to pin.
upstream-api: kubeovn.io/v1

engine: https://github.com/ovn-org/ovn

See ../kube-ovn-vpc/SOURCE.

The Subnet CRD, its controller write-back and the dual-stack cidrBlock convention are all recorded
there, because a Subnet and a Vpc are reconciled by the same controller binary and reading one
without the other would have been half a review. The facts that bear hardest on THIS chart:

  * Subnet is +kubebuilder:resource:scope="Cluster" (pkg/apis/kubeovn/v1/subnet.go).
  * The Subnet CRD declares ZERO defaults. The `default:` lines in its schema are a property NAMED
    `default` (SubnetSpec.Default bool), which is a trap that was checked rather than assumed.
  * formatSubnet/formatAddress rewrite provider, vpc, gatewayType, enableLb, gateway, excludeIps and
    protocol, and CANONICALIZE cidrBlock through net.ParseCIDR. That is why Matches is containment
    and why the CIDR is compared as parsed networks.
  * An empty spec.vpc is filled with the CLUSTER ROUTER — the platform own default VPC — so an
    unbound tenant subnet is not inert.
